    </div>

    <!-- ==================== STRINGS ==================== -->
    <div id="strings">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-emerald-400">S</span>
            Strings
        </h2>

        <!-- SET -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-emerald-400">SET</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Set a key to a string value with optional flags and expiry.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SET key value [NX|XX] [GET] [EX seconds | PX milliseconds | EXAT unix-seconds | PXAT unix-ms | KEEPTTL]</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">
                <span class="text-slate-400">NX</span> &mdash; only set if key does not exist.
                <span class="text-slate-400">XX</span> &mdash; only set if key exists.
                <span class="text-slate-400">GET</span> &mdash; return the old value.
                <span class="text-slate-400">EX/PX</span> &mdash; set TTL in seconds/milliseconds.
                <span class="text-slate-400">EXAT/PXAT</span> &mdash; expire at a Unix time.
                <span class="text-slate-400">KEEPTTL</span> &mdash; keep the existing TTL.
            </div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET mykey hello</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET mykey world NX</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(nil)</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET session token123 EX 3600</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET mykey newval GET</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"hello"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- GET -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-emerald-400">GET</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Get the value of a key. Returns nil if the key does not exist.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GET key</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET greeting "hello world"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GET greeting</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"hello world"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GET nonexistent</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(nil)</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SETNX -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-emerald-400">SETNX</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Set key only if it does not exist. Returns 1 if set, 0 if key already existed.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SETNX key value</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SETNX lock owner1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SETNX lock owner2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SETEX / PSETEX -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-emerald-400">SETEX / PSETEX</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Set key with an expiry. SETEX uses seconds, PSETEX uses milliseconds.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SETEX key seconds value<br>PSETEX key milliseconds value</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SETEX cache:page 60 "&lt;html&gt;..."</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">TTL cache:page</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 60</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- GETSET -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-emerald-400">GETSET</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Atomically set a new value and return the old value.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GETSET key value</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET counter 10</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GETSET counter 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"10"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- MSET / MSETNX / MGET -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-emerald-400">MSET / MSETNX / MGET</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Multi-key operations. MSET sets multiple keys atomically. MSETNX only if none exist. MGET returns multiple values.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">MSET key value [key value ...]<br>MSETNX key value [key value ...]<br>MGET key [key ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">MSET a 1 b 2 c 3</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">MGET a b c</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "1"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "2"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "3"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">MSETNX x 10 y 20 a 99</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Failed because 'a' already exists</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- APPEND / STRLEN -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-emerald-400">APPEND / STRLEN</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">APPEND adds to the end of a string. STRLEN returns the length.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">APPEND key value<br>STRLEN key</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET msg "hello"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">APPEND msg " world"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 11</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">STRLEN msg</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 11</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- INCR / DECR / INCRBY / DECRBY / INCRBYFLOAT -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-emerald-400">INCR / DECR / INCRBY / DECRBY / INCRBYFLOAT</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Atomic numeric operations. Auto-creates key with value 0 if it doesn't exist.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">INCR key<br>DECR key<br>INCRBY key amount<br>DECRBY key amount<br>INCRBYFLOAT key amount</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">INCR views</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">INCRBY views 100</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 101</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">DECRBY views 50</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 51</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET price 10.50</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">INCRBYFLOAT price 2.75</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"13.25"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- GETDEL / GETEX -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-emerald-400">GETDEL / GETEX</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">GETDEL returns and deletes the value atomically. GETEX returns value and optionally sets expiry.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GETDEL key<br>GETEX key [EX seconds | PX milliseconds | EXAT unix-seconds | PXAT unix-ms | PERSIST]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET temp "value"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GETDEL temp</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"value"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GET temp</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(nil)</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET session "data"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GETEX session EX 3600</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"data"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- GETRANGE / SETRANGE -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-emerald-400">GETRANGE / SETRANGE</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">GETRANGE returns a substring. SETRANGE overwrites bytes starting at offset.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GETRANGE key start end<br>SETRANGE key offset value</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET greeting "hello world"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GETRANGE greeting 0 4</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"hello"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GETRANGE greeting -5 -1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"world"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SETRANGE greeting 6 "rust"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 11</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GET greeting</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"hello rustd"</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== LISTS ==================== -->
    <div id="lists">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-cyan-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-cyan-400">L</span>
            Lists
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-8">Backed by a VecDeque &mdash; O(1) push/pop at both ends, O(1) random access.</p>

        <!-- LPUSH / RPUSH -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-cyan-400">LPUSH / RPUSH</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Push elements to the head (LPUSH) or tail (RPUSH) of a list. Creates the list if it doesn't exist. Returns the new length.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">LPUSH key value [value ...]<br>RPUSH key value [value ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">RPUSH queue job1 job2 job3</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LPUSH queue urgent</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 4</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LRANGE queue 0 -1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "urgent"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "job1"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "job2"</div>
                <div class="text-white">4) "job3"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- LPOP / RPOP -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-cyan-400">LPOP / RPOP</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Remove and return an element from the head (LPOP) or tail (RPOP). Returns nil if empty. Optional count removes multiple elements.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">LPOP key [count]<br>RPOP key [count]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">RPUSH tasks a b c d e</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 5</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LPOP tasks</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"a"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">RPOP tasks 2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "e"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "d"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- LLEN / LRANGE / LINDEX / LSET -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-cyan-400">LLEN / LRANGE / LINDEX / LSET</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Query and modify list elements. Negative indices count from the tail (-1 is last).</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">LLEN key<br>LRANGE key start stop<br>LINDEX key index<br>LSET key index value</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">RPUSH colors red green blue</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LLEN colors</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LINDEX colors -1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"blue"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LSET colors 1 yellow</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LRANGE colors 0 -1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "red"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "yellow"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "blue"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- LREM / LTRIM / LINSERT / LPOS -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-cyan-400">LREM / LTRIM / LINSERT / LPOS</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Advanced list manipulation.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">LREM key count value<br>LTRIM key start stop<br>LINSERT key BEFORE|AFTER pivot value<br>LPOS key element [RANK rank] [COUNT n] [MAXLEN len]</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">
                <span class="text-slate-400">LREM count&gt;0</span> &mdash; remove first N from head.
                <span class="text-slate-400">count&lt;0</span> &mdash; remove first N from tail.
                <span class="text-slate-400">count=0</span> &mdash; remove all.
            </div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">RPUSH mylist a b c b d</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 5</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LREM mylist 1 b</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LPOS mylist d</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LINSERT mylist BEFORE c X</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 5</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LTRIM mylist 0 2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LRANGE mylist 0 -1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "a"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "X"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "c"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-cyan-400">LMOVE / RPOPLPUSH / LMPOP / LPUSHX / RPUSHX</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Move an element between lists atomically (across shards too), pop from the first non-empty list, or push only to an existing list.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">LMOVE source destination LEFT|RIGHT LEFT|RIGHT<br>RPOPLPUSH source destination<br>LMPOP numkeys key [key ...] LEFT|RIGHT [COUNT count]<br>LPUSHX key element [element ...]<br>RPUSHX key element [element ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">RPUSH jobs j1 j2 j3</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LMOVE jobs inflight LEFT RIGHT</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"j1"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LMPOP 2 empty jobs RIGHT COUNT 2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "jobs"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) 1) "j3"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2) "j2"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LPUSHX nolist x</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-cyan-400">BLPOP / BRPOP / BLMOVE / BRPOPLPUSH / BLMPOP</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Blocking pops. When every list is empty the client waits up to <code class="text-slate-300">timeout</code> seconds (0 = forever, fractions allowed); clients blocked on the same key are served first come, first served. Inside MULTI or a script they behave like the non-blocking form. <code class="text-slate-300">CLIENT UNBLOCK</code> releases a waiting client.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">BLPOP key [key ...] timeout<br>BRPOP key [key ...] timeout<br>BLMOVE source destination LEFT|RIGHT LEFT|RIGHT timeout<br>BRPOPLPUSH source destination timeout<br>BLMPOP timeout numkeys key [key ...] LEFT|RIGHT [COUNT count]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">RPUSH q task1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">BLPOP q other 5</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "q"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "task1"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">BLPOP q 0.1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(nil)</div>
                <div class="text-slate-500"># with nothing to pop, the client waits; the timeout ends it with nil</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== HASHES ==================== -->
    <div id="hashes">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-purple-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-purple-400">H</span>
            Hashes
        </h2>

        <!-- HSET / HGET / HDEL / HEXISTS -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-purple-400">HSET / HGET / HDEL / HEXISTS</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Basic hash field operations. HSET can set multiple fields at once.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">HSET key field value [field value ...]<br>HGET key field<br>HDEL key field [field ...]<br>HEXISTS key field</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HSET user:1 name Alice age 30 city NYC</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HGET user:1 name</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"Alice"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HEXISTS user:1 age</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HDEL user:1 city</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- HGETALL / HKEYS / HVALS / HLEN / HMSET / HMGET / HINCRBY / HINCRBYFLOAT -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-purple-400">HGETALL / HKEYS / HVALS / HLEN / HMSET / HMGET / HINCRBY / HINCRBYFLOAT</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Bulk hash operations and introspection.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">HGETALL key<br>HKEYS key<br>HVALS key<br>HLEN key<br>HMSET key field val [field val ...]<br>HMGET key field [field ...]<br>HINCRBY key field amount<br>HINCRBYFLOAT key field amount</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HGETALL user:1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "name"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "Alice"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "age"</div>
                <div class="text-white">4) "30"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HKEYS user:1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "name"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "age"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HINCRBY user:1 age 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 31</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HINCRBYFLOAT user:1 score 5.5</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"5.5"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HMGET user:1 name age email</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "Alice"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "31"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) (nil)</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- HSETNX / HSCAN -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-purple-400">HSETNX / HSCAN</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">HSETNX sets a field only if it doesn't exist. HSCAN iterates over hash fields.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">HSETNX key field value<br>HSCAN key cursor [MATCH pattern] [COUNT count]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HSET user:1 name Alice</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HSETNX user:1 name Bob</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HSCAN user:1 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) 1) "name"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2) "Alice"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-purple-400">HSTRLEN / HRANDFIELD</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Length of a field's value; random fields (a negative count may repeat fields).</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">HSTRLEN key field<br>HRANDFIELD key [count [WITHVALUES]]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HSET product name "Widget" sku W-1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HSTRLEN product name</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 6</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-purple-400">HEXPIRE / HPEXPIRE / HEXPIREAT / HPEXPIREAT / HTTL / HPTTL / HEXPIRETIME / HPEXPIRETIME / HPERSIST</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Expiry per hash field (Redis 7.4). Each command takes <code class="text-slate-300">FIELDS numfields field ...</code> and answers one code per field: <code class="text-slate-300">-2</code> no such field, <code class="text-slate-300">0</code> condition not met, <code class="text-slate-300">1</code> set, <code class="text-slate-300">2</code> deleted because the time is already past.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">HEXPIRE key seconds [NX | XX | GT | LT] FIELDS numfields field [field ...]<br>HPEXPIRE key milliseconds [NX | XX | GT | LT] FIELDS numfields field [field ...]<br>HEXPIREAT key unix-seconds [NX | XX | GT | LT] FIELDS numfields field [field ...]<br>HTTL key FIELDS numfields field [field ...]<br>HPERSIST key FIELDS numfields field [field ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HSET session user alice token abc</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HEXPIRE session 60 FIELDS 2 token missing</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) (integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) (integer) -2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HTTL session FIELDS 2 token user</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) (integer) 60</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) (integer) -1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HPERSIST session FIELDS 1 token</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) (integer) 1</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-purple-400">HGETDEL / HGETEX / HSETEX</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Redis 8's field commands: read and delete, read and set or clear expiry, and set fields with expiry all-or-nothing (<code class="text-slate-300">FNX</code>: none may exist, <code class="text-slate-300">FXX</code>: all must).</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">HGETDEL key FIELDS numfields field [field ...]<br>HGETEX key [EX seconds | PX ms | EXAT unix-seconds | PXAT unix-ms | PERSIST] FIELDS numfields field [field ...]<br>HSETEX key [FNX | FXX] [EX seconds | PX ms | EXAT unix-seconds | PXAT unix-ms | KEEPTTL] FIELDS numfields field value [field value ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HSETEX cart EX 3600 FIELDS 2 item1 2 item2 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HGETDEL cart FIELDS 1 item1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "2"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HGETEX cart PERSIST FIELDS 1 item2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "1"</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== SETS ==================== -->
    <div id="sets">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-pink-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-pink-400">S</span>
            Sets
        </h2>

        <!-- SADD / SREM / SMEMBERS / SISMEMBER / SCARD -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-pink-400">SADD / SREM / SMEMBERS / SISMEMBER / SCARD</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Basic set operations.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SADD key member [member ...]<br>SREM key member [member ...]<br>SMEMBERS key<br>SISMEMBER key member<br>SCARD key</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SADD tags redis nosql fast</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SISMEMBER tags redis</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SCARD tags</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SMEMBERS tags</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "fast"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "nosql"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "redis"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SPOP / SRANDMEMBER / SUNION / SINTER / SDIFF / SMOVE -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-pink-400">SPOP / SRANDMEMBER / SUNION / SINTER / SDIFF / SMOVE</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Random access and set algebra. SMOVE moves a member between sets.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SPOP key [count]<br>SRANDMEMBER key [count]<br>SUNION key [key ...]<br>SINTER key [key ...]<br>SDIFF key [key ...]<br>SMOVE source destination member</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SADD s1 a b c d</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 4</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SADD s2 c d e f</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 4</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SINTER s1 s2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "c"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "d"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SDIFF s1 s2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "a"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "b"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SMOVE s1 s2 a</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SMEMBERS s2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "a"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "c"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "d"</div>
                <div class="text-white">4) "e"</div>
                <div class="text-white">5) "f"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-pink-400">SMISMEMBER / SINTERCARD / SINTERSTORE / SUNIONSTORE / SDIFFSTORE / SSCAN</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Membership of several members at once, intersection size with an early stop, set algebra stored into a key, and cursor iteration.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SMISMEMBER key member [member ...]<br>SINTERCARD numkeys key [key ...] [LIMIT limit]<br>SINTERSTORE destination key [key ...]<br>SUNIONSTORE destination key [key ...]<br>SDIFFSTORE destination key [key ...]<br>SSCAN key cursor [MATCH pattern] [COUNT count]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SADD {t}a x y z</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SADD {t}b y z w</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SMISMEMBER {t}a x w</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) (integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) (integer) 0</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SINTERCARD 2 {t}a {t}b</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SINTERSTORE {t}both {t}a {t}b</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== SORTED SETS ==================== -->
    <div id="sorted-sets">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-orange-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-orange-400">Z</span>
            Sorted Sets
        </h2>

        <!-- ZADD / ZREM / ZSCORE / ZRANK / ZREVRANK -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-orange-400">ZADD / ZREM / ZSCORE / ZRANK / ZREVRANK</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Add scored members and query individual scores/ranks.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">ZADD key [NX|XX] [GT|LT] [CH] [INCR] score member [score member ...]<br>ZREM key member [member ...]<br>ZSCORE key member<br>ZRANK key member<br>ZREVRANK key member</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZADD leaderboard 100 alice 200 bob 150 charlie</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZSCORE leaderboard bob</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"200"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZRANK leaderboard alice</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># alice has the lowest score, so rank 0</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZREVRANK leaderboard alice</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs"># alice is last when sorted high-to-low</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ZRANGE / ZREVRANGE / ZRANGEBYSCORE -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-orange-400">ZRANGE / ZREVRANGE / ZRANGEBYSCORE</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Range queries by rank or score. Use WITHSCORES to include scores. Use -inf/+inf for open ranges.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">ZRANGE key start stop [BYSCORE | BYLEX] [REV] [LIMIT offset count] [WITHSCORES]<br>ZREVRANGE key start stop [WITHSCORES]<br>ZRANGEBYSCORE key min max [WITHSCORES] [LIMIT offset count]<br>ZREVRANGEBYSCORE key max min [WITHSCORES] [LIMIT offset count]</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">Score bounds accept <span class="text-slate-400">-inf</span>, <span class="text-slate-400">+inf</span> and exclusive <span class="text-slate-400">(</span> bounds, e.g. <span class="text-slate-400">(100</span>. Lex bounds use <span class="text-slate-400">[a</span>, <span class="text-slate-400">(a</span>, <span class="text-slate-400">-</span> and <span class="text-slate-400">+</span>.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZRANGE leaderboard 0 -1 WITHSCORES</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "alice"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "100"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "charlie"</div>
                <div class="text-white">4) "150"</div>
                <div class="text-white">5) "bob"</div>
                <div class="text-white">6) "200"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZRANGEBYSCORE leaderboard 100 160</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "alice"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "charlie"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZREVRANGE leaderboard 0 0 WITHSCORES</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "bob"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "200"</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Top scorer</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ZCARD / ZCOUNT / ZINCRBY / ZREMRANGEBYSCORE -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-orange-400">ZCARD / ZCOUNT / ZINCRBY / ZREMRANGEBYSCORE</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Counting, incrementing, and bulk removal.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">ZCARD key<br>ZCOUNT key min max<br>ZINCRBY key increment member<br>ZREMRANGEBYSCORE key min max</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZCARD leaderboard</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZCOUNT leaderboard 100 200</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZINCRBY leaderboard 50 alice</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"150"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZREMRANGEBYSCORE leaderboard -inf 100</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs"># No members with score &lt;= 100 after ZINCRBY</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ZPOPMIN / ZPOPMAX -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-orange-400">ZPOPMIN / ZPOPMAX</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Remove and return the lowest/highest scoring members.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">ZPOPMIN key [count]<br>ZPOPMAX key [count]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZADD prices 10 apple 30 banana 20 cherry</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZPOPMIN prices 2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "apple"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "10"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "cherry"</div>
                <div class="text-white">4) "20"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZPOPMAX prices</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "banana"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "30"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ZUNIONSTORE / ZINTERSTORE -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-orange-400">ZUNIONSTORE / ZINTERSTORE</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Store the union/intersection of sorted sets with optional weights and aggregation.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">ZUNIONSTORE dest numkeys key [key ...] [WEIGHTS weight ...] [AGGREGATE SUM|MIN|MAX]<br>ZINTERSTORE dest numkeys key [key ...] [WEIGHTS weight ...] [AGGREGATE SUM|MIN|MAX]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZADD z1 1 a 2 b</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZADD z2 1 b 2 c</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZUNIONSTORE result 2 z1 z2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZRANGE result 0 -1 WITHSCORES</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "a"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "1"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "c"</div>
                <div class="text-white">4) "2"</div>
                <div class="text-white">5) "b"</div>
                <div class="text-white">6) "3"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ZSCAN -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-orange-400">ZSCAN</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Iterate over members in a sorted set.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">ZSCAN key cursor [MATCH pattern] [COUNT count]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZSCAN leaderboard 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) 1) "alice"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2) "100"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;3) "bob"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;4) "200"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-orange-400">ZRANGEBYLEX / ZREVRANGEBYLEX / ZLEXCOUNT / ZREMRANGEBYLEX / ZREMRANGEBYRANK</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Lexicographic ranges over members that share a score, and removal by rank.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">ZRANGEBYLEX key min max [LIMIT offset count]<br>ZREVRANGEBYLEX key max min [LIMIT offset count]<br>ZLEXCOUNT key min max<br>ZREMRANGEBYLEX key min max<br>ZREMRANGEBYRANK key start stop</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZADD names 0 alice 0 bob 0 carol 0 dave</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 4</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZRANGEBYLEX names [b (d</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "bob"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "carol"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZLEXCOUNT names - +</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 4</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZREMRANGEBYRANK names 0 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-orange-400">BZPOPMIN / BZPOPMAX / ZMPOP / BZMPOP</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Pop the lowest or highest members, optionally blocking until one is available.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">BZPOPMIN key [key ...] timeout<br>BZPOPMAX key [key ...] timeout<br>ZMPOP numkeys key [key ...] MIN|MAX [COUNT count]<br>BZMPOP timeout numkeys key [key ...] MIN|MAX [COUNT count]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZADD prio 1 low 5 high</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">BZPOPMAX prio 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "prio"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "high"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "5"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZMPOP 1 prio MIN</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "prio"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) 1) 1) "low"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2) "1"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-orange-400">ZUNION / ZINTER / ZDIFF / ZDIFFSTORE / ZINTERCARD / ZRANGESTORE / ZMSCORE / ZRANDMEMBER</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Set algebra returned directly, stored range queries, several scores at once, and random members.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">ZUNION numkeys key [key ...] [WEIGHTS w ...] [AGGREGATE SUM|MIN|MAX] [WITHSCORES]<br>ZINTER numkeys key [key ...] [WEIGHTS w ...] [AGGREGATE SUM|MIN|MAX] [WITHSCORES]<br>ZDIFF numkeys key [key ...] [WITHSCORES]<br>ZDIFFSTORE destination numkeys key [key ...]<br>ZINTERCARD numkeys key [key ...] [LIMIT limit]<br>ZRANGESTORE dst src min max [BYSCORE | BYLEX] [REV] [LIMIT offset count]<br>ZMSCORE key member [member ...]<br>ZRANDMEMBER key [count [WITHSCORES]]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZADD {z}a 1 x 2 y</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZADD {z}b 10 y 20 z</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZINTER 2 {z}a {z}b WITHSCORES</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "y"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "12"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZMSCORE {z}a x nope</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "1"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) (nil)</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZRANGESTORE {z}top {z}b 0 0 REV</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== STREAMS ==================== -->
    <div id="streams">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-sky-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-sky-400">S</span>
            Streams
        </h2>

        <!-- XADD / XLEN -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-sky-400">XADD / XLEN</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Append entries to a stream and query its length. Use <code class="text-slate-300">*</code> for auto-generated IDs. NOMKSTREAM prevents creating a new stream. MAXLEN/MINID trim older entries on write.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">XADD key [NOMKSTREAM] [MAXLEN|MINID [=|~] N] *|id field value [field value ...]<br>XLEN key</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XADD events * user alice action login</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"1709000000000-0"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XADD events * user bob action purchase item hat</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"1709000000001-0"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XADD events MAXLEN 1000 * user charlie action logout</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"1709000000002-0"</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Trims stream to 1000 entries after adding</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XLEN events</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- XRANGE / XREVRANGE -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-sky-400">XRANGE / XREVRANGE</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Query entries by ID range. Use <code class="text-slate-300">-</code> for minimum and <code class="text-slate-300">+</code> for maximum. XREVRANGE returns entries in reverse order. COUNT limits results.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">XRANGE key start end [COUNT n]<br>XREVRANGE key end start [COUNT n]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XRANGE events - +</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) 1) "1709000000000-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "user" 2) "alice" 3) "action" 4) "login"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) 1) "1709000000001-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "user" 2) "bob" 3) "action" 4) "purchase" 5) "item" 6) "hat"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) 1) "1709000000002-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "user" 2) "charlie" 3) "action" 4) "logout"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XRANGE events 1709000000001-0 + COUNT 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) 1) "1709000000001-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "user" 2) "bob" 3) "action" 4) "purchase" 5) "item" 6) "hat"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XREVRANGE events + - COUNT 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) 1) "1709000000002-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "user" 2) "charlie" 3) "action" 4) "logout"</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Most recent entry</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- XREAD -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-sky-400">XREAD</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Read new entries from one or more streams after the given IDs. Use <code class="text-slate-300">0-0</code> to read from the beginning. BLOCK is accepted but returns immediately in v1.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">XREAD [COUNT n] [BLOCK ms] STREAMS key [key ...] id [id ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XREAD COUNT 2 STREAMS events 0-0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) 1) "events"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) 1) "1709000000000-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "user" 2) "alice" 3) "action" 4) "login"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "1709000000001-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "user" 2) "bob" 3) "action" 4) "purchase" 5) "item" 6) "hat"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XREAD STREAMS events 1709000000002-0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(nil)</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># No entries after the last ID</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- XDEL / XTRIM -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-sky-400">XDEL / XTRIM</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Remove specific entries or trim the stream. MAXLEN caps the total number of entries. MINID removes entries below a threshold ID. Use <code class="text-slate-300">~</code> for approximate trimming.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">XDEL key id [id ...]<br>XTRIM key MAXLEN|MINID [=|~] N</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XDEL events 1709000000000-0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XLEN events</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XTRIM events MAXLEN 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Removed 1 entry, stream now has 1 entry</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XTRIM events MINID 1709000000003-0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs"># Removed entries older than the given ID</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- XINFO -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-sky-400">XINFO</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Introspect stream metadata: length, first/last entry, consumer group count, and last generated ID.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">XINFO STREAM key</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XADD logs * level info msg "server started"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"1709000000000-0"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XINFO STREAM logs</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;1) "length"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;2) (integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;3) "first-entry"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;4) 1) "1709000000000-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "level" 2) "info" 3) "msg" 4) "server started"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;5) "last-entry"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;6) 1) "1709000000000-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "level" 2) "info" 3) "msg" 4) "server started"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;7) "groups"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;8) (integer) 0</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;9) "last-generated-id"</div>
                <div class="text-white">10) "1709000000000-0"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- XGROUP CREATE / DESTROY / DELCONSUMER -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-sky-400">XGROUP CREATE / DESTROY / DELCONSUMER</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Manage consumer groups. CREATE attaches a group to a stream starting from a given ID (<code class="text-slate-300">0</code> = all history, <code class="text-slate-300">$</code> = new entries only). MKSTREAM creates the stream if it doesn't exist. DELCONSUMER removes a consumer and its pending entries.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">XGROUP CREATE key group id|$ [MKSTREAM]<br>XGROUP DESTROY key group<br>XGROUP DELCONSUMER key group consumer</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XGROUP CREATE events workers 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Group "workers" reads all existing entries</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XGROUP CREATE newstream analytics $ MKSTREAM</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs"># Creates the stream + group, reads only new entries</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XGROUP DELCONSUMER events workers consumer1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs"># Returns the number of pending entries that were deleted</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XGROUP DESTROY events workers</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- XREADGROUP -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-sky-400">XREADGROUP</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Read entries via a consumer group. Use <code class="text-slate-300">&gt;</code> to get new undelivered entries. Use <code class="text-slate-300">0</code> to re-read your own pending entries. Each delivered entry is tracked until acknowledged with XACK.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">XREADGROUP GROUP group consumer [COUNT n] [BLOCK ms] STREAMS key [key ...] id [id ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XADD tasks * job build</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"1709000000000-0"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XADD tasks * job test</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"1709000000001-0"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XGROUP CREATE tasks ci 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XREADGROUP GROUP ci runner1 COUNT 1 STREAMS tasks &gt;</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) 1) "tasks"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) 1) "1709000000000-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "job" 2) "build"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XREADGROUP GROUP ci runner1 COUNT 10 STREAMS tasks &gt;</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) 1) "tasks"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) 1) "1709000000001-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) 1) "job" 2) "test"</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Each call delivers the next undelivered entry</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XREADGROUP GROUP ci runner1 STREAMS tasks 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs"># Re-reads all pending entries for runner1</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- XACK -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-sky-400">XACK</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Acknowledge processed entries. Removes them from the consumer's pending list. Returns the number of entries successfully acknowledged.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">XACK key group id [id ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XACK tasks ci 1709000000000-0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XACK tasks ci 1709000000000-0 1709000000001-0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># First ID was already acked, only second counts</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- XPENDING -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-sky-400">XPENDING</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Inspect pending entries. Summary form shows total count, min/max ID, and per-consumer counts. Detail form shows individual entries with idle time and delivery count.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">XPENDING key group<br>XPENDING key group start end count [consumer]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XPENDING tasks ci</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) (integer) 2</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "1709000000000-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "1709000000001-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">4) 1) 1) "runner1"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) "2"</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Summary: 2 pending, min/max IDs, runner1 has 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XPENDING tasks ci - + 10</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) 1) "1709000000000-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) "runner1"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 3) (integer) 5000</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 4) (integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) 1) "1709000000001-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 2) "runner1"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 3) (integer) 3000</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp; 4) (integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Detail: ID, consumer, idle ms, delivery count</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XPENDING tasks ci - + 10 runner1</span></div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs"># Same but filtered to a specific consumer</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-sky-400">XCLAIM / XAUTOCLAIM / XSETID</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Recover pending entries from consumers that died: claim given IDs, or scan the pending list for entries idle longer than a threshold. Delivery times and counts survive restarts and reach replicas.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">XCLAIM key group consumer min-idle-time id [id ...] [IDLE ms] [TIME unix-ms] [RETRYCOUNT n] [FORCE] [JUSTID] [LASTID id]<br>XAUTOCLAIM key group consumer min-idle-time start [COUNT count] [JUSTID]<br>XSETID key last-id [ENTRIESADDED n] [MAXDELETEDID id]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XGROUP CREATE orders billing $ MKSTREAM</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div class="text-slate-500"># … a consumer reads with XREADGROUP and never acknowledges …</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">XAUTOCLAIM orders billing worker-2 60000 0-0 COUNT 10</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "0-0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) (empty array)</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) (empty array)</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== KEYS ==================== -->
    <div id="keys">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-yellow-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-yellow-400">K</span>
            Keys
        </h2>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-yellow-400">DEL / UNLINK / EXISTS / TYPE / RENAME / RENAMENX</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Key management. UNLINK is async alternative to DEL. These work across all data types.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">DEL key [key ...]<br>UNLINK key [key ...]<br>EXISTS key [key ...]<br>TYPE key<br>RENAME key newkey<br>RENAMENX key newkey</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET foo bar</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">TYPE foo</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">string</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">EXISTS foo</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">RENAME foo baz</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">UNLINK baz</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-yellow-400">EXPIRE / PEXPIRE / EXPIREAT / PEXPIREAT / TTL / PTTL / PERSIST / KEYS</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">TTL management and key search. EXPIRE/PEXPIRE set relative TTL. EXPIREAT/PEXPIREAT set absolute timestamp.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">EXPIRE key seconds [NX | XX | GT | LT]<br>PEXPIRE key milliseconds [NX | XX | GT | LT]<br>EXPIREAT key unix-seconds [NX | XX | GT | LT]<br>PEXPIREAT key unix-ms [NX | XX | GT | LT]<br>EXPIRETIME key<br>PEXPIRETIME key<br>TTL key<br>PTTL key<br>PERSIST key<br>KEYS pattern</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3"><span class="text-slate-400">NX</span> &mdash; only if the key has no TTL. <span class="text-slate-400">XX</span> &mdash; only if it has one. <span class="text-slate-400">GT/LT</span> &mdash; only if the new TTL is greater/less. A TTL that is zero, negative or in the past deletes the key.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET temp hello</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">EXPIRE temp 30</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">TTL temp</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 30</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">PERSIST temp</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">KEYS user:*</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "user:1"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-yellow-400">SCAN / RANDOMKEY / OBJECT</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Key iteration and introspection. SCAN iterates keys without blocking and returns every key present for the whole iteration; on a multi-shard server the cursor walks shard by shard, so keep calling until it returns "0". SCAN also takes TYPE. OBJECT reports encoding, idle time and frequency.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SCAN cursor [MATCH pattern] [COUNT count] [TYPE type]<br>RANDOMKEY<br>OBJECT ENCODING|IDLETIME|FREQ|REFCOUNT key</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SCAN 0 MATCH user:* COUNT 100</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) 1) "user:1"</div>
                <div class="text-white">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2) "user:2"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">RANDOMKEY</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"user:1"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">OBJECT ENCODING mystring</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"embstr"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-yellow-400">COPY / MOVE / TOUCH / SORT / SORT_RO / DUMP / RESTORE</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Copy or move keys between databases, refresh access time, sort lists/sets/sorted sets, and serialize values. <code class="text-slate-300">DUMP</code> payloads use Redis' format for strings, lists, sets, hashes and sorted sets, so they restore into Redis and back.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">COPY source destination [DB index] [REPLACE]<br>MOVE key db<br>TOUCH key [key ...]<br>SORT key [BY pattern] [LIMIT offset count] [GET pattern ...] [ASC|DESC] [ALPHA] [STORE destination]<br>SORT_RO key [BY pattern] [LIMIT offset count] [GET pattern ...] [ASC|DESC] [ALPHA]<br>DUMP key<br>RESTORE key ttl serialized-value [REPLACE] [ABSTTL] [IDLETIME s] [FREQ f]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">RPUSH nums 3 1 2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SORT nums</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "1"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "2"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) "3"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">COPY nums nums-copy</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">MOVE nums-copy 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== TRANSACTIONS ==================== -->
    <div id="transactions">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-red-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-red-400">T</span>
            Transactions
        </h2>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-red-400">MULTI / EXEC / DISCARD / WATCH / UNWATCH</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Queue commands with MULTI, then execute atomically with EXEC: the shards of every queued and watched key are locked for the duration, so no other client interleaves. WATCH makes EXEC return nil if a watched key changed (write, expiry, flush) before it ran. A queued command with an unknown name or wrong argument count aborts the transaction with EXECABORT. DISCARD drops the queue and the watches.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">MULTI<br>EXEC<br>DISCARD<br>WATCH key [key ...]<br>UNWATCH</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">MULTI</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET account:1:balance 500</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">QUEUED</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET account:2:balance 1500</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">QUEUED</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">EXEC</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) OK</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) OK</div>
                <div class="mt-2"><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">MULTI</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET x 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">QUEUED</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">DISCARD</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Transaction aborted, x was not set</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== PUB/SUB ==================== -->
    <div id="pubsub">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-teal-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-teal-400">P</span>
            Pub/Sub
        </h2>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-teal-400">SUBSCRIBE / UNSUBSCRIBE / PUBLISH / PSUBSCRIBE / PUNSUBSCRIBE / PUBSUB</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Publish-subscribe messaging. PSUBSCRIBE supports glob patterns. PUBSUB provides introspection.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SUBSCRIBE channel [channel ...]<br>UNSUBSCRIBE [channel ...]<br>PUBLISH channel message<br>PSUBSCRIBE pattern [pattern ...]<br>PUNSUBSCRIBE [pattern ...]<br>PUBSUB CHANNELS [pattern]<br>PUBSUB NUMSUB [channel ...]</div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <div>
                    <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 uppercase mb-2">Terminal 1 (subscriber)</div>
                    <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                        <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SUBSCRIBE news</span></div>
                        <div class="text-white">1) "subscribe"</div>
                        <div class="text-white">2) "news"</div>
                        <div class="text-white">3) (integer) 1</div>
                        <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Waiting for messages...</div>
                        <div class="text-white mt-2">1) "message"</div>
                        <div class="text-white">2) "news"</div>
                        <div class="text-white">3) "breaking: SoliKV released"</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 uppercase mb-2">Terminal 2 (publisher)</div>
                    <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                        <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">PUBLISH news "breaking: SoliKV released"</span></div>
                        <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                        <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># 1 subscriber received it</div>
                        <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">PUBSUB CHANNELS</span></div>
                        <div class="text-white">1) "news"</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Keyspace Notifications -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-teal-400">Keyspace Notifications</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">
                Enable event-driven notifications when keys are modified, deleted, or expire.
                Clients subscribe via PSUBSCRIBE to channels like <code class="text-slate-300">__keyevent@0__:expired</code> or <code class="text-slate-300">__keyspace@0__:mykey</code>.
                Disabled by default &mdash; enable with <code class="text-slate-300">CONFIG SET notify-keyspace-events</code>.
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">
                <span class="text-slate-400">K</span> &mdash; keyspace events (<code class="text-slate-300">__keyspace@0__:&lt;key&gt;</code>).
                <span class="text-slate-400">E</span> &mdash; keyevent events (<code class="text-slate-300">__keyevent@0__:&lt;event&gt;</code>).
                <span class="text-slate-400">g</span> &mdash; generic commands (DEL, EXPIRE, RENAME...).
                <span class="text-slate-400">$</span> &mdash; string commands.
                <span class="text-slate-400">l</span> &mdash; list commands.
                <span class="text-slate-400">s</span> &mdash; set commands.
                <span class="text-slate-400">h</span> &mdash; hash commands.
                <span class="text-slate-400">z</span> &mdash; sorted set commands.
                <span class="text-slate-400">t</span> &mdash; stream commands.
                <span class="text-slate-400">x</span> &mdash; expired events.
                <span class="text-slate-400">e</span> &mdash; evicted events.
                <span class="text-slate-400">A</span> &mdash; alias for g$lshztxe (all events).
            </div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">CONFIG SET notify-keyspace-events KEA</div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                <div>
                    <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 uppercase mb-2">Terminal 1 (subscriber)</div>
                    <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                        <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">PSUBSCRIBE __keyevent@0__:*</span></div>
                        <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># Waiting for events...</div>
                        <div class="text-white mt-2">1) "pmessage"</div>
                        <div class="text-white">2) "__keyevent@0__:*"</div>
                        <div class="text-white">3) "__keyevent@0__:set"</div>
                        <div class="text-white">4) "mykey"</div>
                        <div class="text-white mt-2">1) "pmessage"</div>
                        <div class="text-white">2) "__keyevent@0__:*"</div>
                        <div class="text-white">3) "__keyevent@0__:expired"</div>
                        <div class="text-white">4) "mykey"</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 uppercase mb-2">Terminal 2 (publisher)</div>
                    <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                        <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">CONFIG SET notify-keyspace-events KEA</span></div>
                        <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                        <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET mykey hello PX 1000</span></div>
                        <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                        <div class="text-slate-600 text-xs mt-1"># After 1 second, expired event fires</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-teal-400">SSUBSCRIBE / SUNSUBSCRIBE / SPUBLISH / PUBSUB SHARDCHANNELS / SHARDNUMSUB</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Sharded pub/sub: channels hash to a slot like keys, so in cluster mode a message only travels to the node that owns it (plain <code class="text-slate-300">PUBLISH</code> reaches every node). Under RESP3 messages arrive as push frames and other commands can run on the same connection.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SSUBSCRIBE shardchannel [shardchannel ...]<br>SUNSUBSCRIBE [shardchannel ...]<br>SPUBLISH shardchannel message<br>PUBSUB SHARDCHANNELS [pattern]<br>PUBSUB SHARDNUMSUB [shardchannel ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SPUBLISH orders:eu "created 42"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== SCRIPTING ==================== -->
    <div id="scripting">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-indigo-400">L</span>
            Scripting
        </h2>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-indigo-400">EVAL</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Execute a Lua script server-side. Scripts receive KEYS and ARGV tables, and can call Redis commands via <code class="text-slate-300">redis.call()</code> and <code class="text-slate-300">redis.pcall()</code>.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">EVAL script numkeys [key ...] [arg ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">EVAL "return 42" 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 42</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">EVAL "return redis.call('SET',KEYS[1],ARGV[1])" 1 mykey myval</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">EVAL "return redis.call('GET',KEYS[1])" 1 mykey</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"myval"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">EVAL "return {1, 2, 3}" 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) (integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) (integer) 2</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) (integer) 3</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-indigo-400">EVALSHA</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Execute a cached script by its SHA1 digest. Use SCRIPT LOAD to cache scripts first. Returns NOSCRIPT error if the script is not cached.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">EVALSHA sha1 numkeys [key ...] [arg ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">EVALSHA 1b936e3fe509bcbc9cd0664897bbe8fd0cac101b 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"hello"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-indigo-400">SCRIPT LOAD</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Cache a Lua script and return its SHA1 digest for later use with EVALSHA.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SCRIPT LOAD script</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SCRIPT LOAD "return 'hello'"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"1b936e3fe509bcbc9cd0664897bbe8fd0cac101b"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-indigo-400">SCRIPT EXISTS</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Check if one or more scripts are cached. Returns an array of 1 (cached) or 0 (not cached) for each SHA1.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SCRIPT EXISTS sha1 [sha1 ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SCRIPT EXISTS 1b936e3fe509bcbc9cd0664897bbe8fd0cac101b 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) (integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) (integer) 0</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-indigo-400">SCRIPT FLUSH</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Clear the script cache. All previously loaded scripts will need to be re-loaded.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SCRIPT FLUSH</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SCRIPT FLUSH</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-indigo-400">EVAL_RO / EVALSHA_RO / SCRIPT KILL / FUNCTION / FCALL / FCALL_RO</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Read-only script variants, stopping a runaway script, and Redis 7 functions. Scripts run Lua 5.1 with <code class="text-slate-300">cjson</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">cmsgpack</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">bit</code> and <code class="text-slate-300">struct</code>; globals and libraries are read-only. A script running past <code class="text-slate-300">--busy-reply-threshold</code> makes other clients get <code class="text-slate-300">-BUSY</code>. Function libraries are stored in snapshots and the log, and replicated.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">EVAL_RO script numkeys [key ...] [arg ...]<br>EVALSHA_RO sha1 numkeys [key ...] [arg ...]<br>SCRIPT LOAD | EXISTS | FLUSH [ASYNC|SYNC] | KILL<br>FUNCTION LOAD [REPLACE] code | DELETE name | FLUSH | LIST [LIBRARYNAME p] [WITHCODE] | DUMP | RESTORE payload | STATS | KILL<br>FCALL function numkeys [key ...] [arg ...]<br>FCALL_RO function numkeys [key ...] [arg ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">EVAL "return cjson.encode({ok=true})" 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"{\"ok\":true}"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">FUNCTION LOAD "#!lua name=util\nredis.register_function('hello', function() return 'hi' end)"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"util"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">FCALL hello 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"hi"</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== BITMAP ==================== -->
    <div id="bitmap">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-amber-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-amber-400">B</span>
            Bitmap
        </h2>

        <!-- SETBIT -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-amber-400">SETBIT</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Set or clear the bit at offset in the string value stored at key. Returns the original bit value. The string is auto-grown with zero bytes to ensure the offset can be addressed.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SETBIT key offset value</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">SETBIT mykey 7 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">SETBIT mykey 7 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- GETBIT -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-amber-400">GETBIT</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Returns the bit value at offset in the string value stored at key. Returns 0 if the key does not exist or the offset is beyond the string length.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GETBIT key offset</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">SETBIT mykey 7 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">GETBIT mykey 7</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">GETBIT mykey 100</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- BITCOUNT -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-amber-400">BITCOUNT</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Count the number of set bits (population counting) in a string. By default examines all bytes; optional start/end specify a byte range (negative indices count from the end).</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">BITCOUNT key [start end]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">SET mykey "\xff\xf0"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">BITCOUNT mykey</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 12</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">BITCOUNT mykey 0 0</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 8</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- BITOP -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-amber-400">BITOP</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Perform a bitwise operation between multiple keys and store the result in the destination key. Supported operations: AND, OR, XOR, NOT. NOT takes exactly one source key. Shorter strings are zero-padded.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">BITOP operation destkey key [key ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">SET k1 "\xff"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">SET k2 "\x0f"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">BITOP AND dest k1 k2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-amber-400">BITOP NOT negated k1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-amber-400">BITPOS / BITFIELD / BITFIELD_RO / LCS</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Find the first set or clear bit, treat a string as an array of integers of any width, and longest common subsequence of two strings.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">BITPOS key bit [start [end [BYTE | BIT]]]<br>BITFIELD key [GET type offset] [SET type offset value] [INCRBY type offset increment] [OVERFLOW WRAP|SAT|FAIL] ...<br>BITFIELD_RO key GET type offset [GET type offset ...]<br>LCS key1 key2 [LEN] [IDX] [MINMATCHLEN n] [WITHMATCHLEN]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SETBIT flags 9 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">BITPOS flags 1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 9</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">BITFIELD counters INCRBY u8 0 200 INCRBY u8 0 100</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) (integer) 200</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) (integer) 44</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">MSET {l}a ohmytext {l}b mynewtext</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">LCS {l}a {l}b</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"mytext"</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== SERVER ==================== -->
    <!-- ==================== HYPERLOGLOG ==================== -->
    <div id="hyperloglog">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-violet-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-violet-400">H</span>
            HyperLogLog
        </h2>

        <!-- PFADD -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-violet-400">PFADD</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Add elements to a HyperLogLog. Returns 1 if any internal register was altered, 0 otherwise.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">PFADD key element [element ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-violet-400">PFADD visitors alice bob charlie alice</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-violet-400">PFADD visitors alice</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- PFCOUNT -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-violet-400">PFCOUNT</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Return the approximate cardinality of the set(s). Multiple keys are merged internally before counting.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">PFCOUNT key [key ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-violet-400">PFCOUNT visitors</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- PFMERGE -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-violet-400">PFMERGE</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Merge multiple HyperLogLogs into a destination key. Creates or overwrites the destination.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">PFMERGE destkey sourcekey [sourcekey ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-violet-400">PFMERGE all visitors1 visitors2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-violet-400">PFCOUNT all</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 5</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== BLOOM FILTER ==================== -->
    <div id="bloom-filter">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-rose-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-rose-400">B</span>
            Bloom Filter
        </h2>

        <!-- BF.RESERVE -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-rose-400">BF.RESERVE</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Create an empty Bloom filter with a given desired error rate and initial capacity. The filter auto-creates with defaults (0.01 error, 100 capacity) on first BF.ADD if not reserved.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">BF.RESERVE key error_rate capacity</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-rose-400">BF.RESERVE myfilter 0.001 10000</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- BF.ADD -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-rose-400">BF.ADD</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Add an item to the Bloom filter. Returns 1 if the item was newly added, 0 if it may have existed.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">BF.ADD key item</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-rose-400">BF.ADD myfilter hello</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- BF.MADD -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-rose-400">BF.MADD</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Add multiple items to the Bloom filter. Returns an array of 1/0 for each item.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">BF.MADD key item [item ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-rose-400">BF.MADD myfilter foo bar baz</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) (integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) (integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) (integer) 1</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- BF.EXISTS -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-rose-400">BF.EXISTS</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Check if an item may exist in the Bloom filter. Returns 1 if it may exist (possible false positive), 0 if it definitely does not.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">BF.EXISTS key item</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-rose-400">BF.EXISTS myfilter hello</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 1</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-rose-400">BF.EXISTS myfilter unknown</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 0</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- BF.MEXISTS -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-rose-400">BF.MEXISTS</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Check if multiple items may exist in the Bloom filter. Returns an array of 1/0 for each item.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">BF.MEXISTS key item [item ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-rose-400">BF.MEXISTS myfilter hello unknown</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) (integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) (integer) 0</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- BF.INFO -->
        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-rose-400">BF.INFO</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Return information about a Bloom filter: capacity, size, number of filters, items inserted, and expansion rate.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">BF.INFO key</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-rose-400">BF.INFO myfilter</span></div>
                <div class="text-white"> 1) "Capacity"</div>
                <div class="text-white"> 2) (integer) 10000</div>
                <div class="text-white"> 3) "Size"</div>
                <div class="text-white"> 4) (integer) 14378</div>
                <div class="text-white"> 5) "Number of filters"</div>
                <div class="text-white"> 6) (integer) 1</div>
                <div class="text-white"> 7) "Number of items inserted"</div>
                <div class="text-white"> 8) (integer) 42</div>
                <div class="text-white"> 9) "Expansion rate"</div>
                <div class="text-white">10) (integer) 0</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="geospatial">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-teal-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-teal-400">G</span>
            Geospatial
        </h2>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-teal-400">GEOADD</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Add one or more geospatial items (longitude, latitude, name) to a sorted set. Items are stored as 52-bit geohash scores.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GEOADD key [NX|XX] [CH] longitude latitude member [longitude latitude member ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GEOADD mygeo 13.361389 38.115556 "Palermo" 15.087269 37.502669 "Catania"</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-teal-400">GEOPOS</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Return the longitude and latitude of one or more members. Returns nil for missing members.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GEOPOS key member [member ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GEOPOS mygeo Palermo</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) 1) "13.36138933897018433"</div>
                <div class="text-white">   2) "38.11555639549629859"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-teal-400">GEOHASH</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Return the standard 11-character geohash string for one or more members.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GEOHASH key member [member ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GEOHASH mygeo Palermo</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "sqc8b49rny0"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-teal-400">GEODIST</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Return the distance between two members. Supports m (meters), km, ft, mi units. Returns nil if either member is missing.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GEODIST key member1 member2 [M|KM|FT|MI]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GEODIST mygeo Palermo Catania km</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"166.2742"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-teal-400">GEOSEARCH</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Search for members within a radius or bounding box from a center point (coordinates or existing member). Supports sorting, counting, and returning coordinates/distances.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GEOSEARCH key FROMMEMBER member | FROMLONLAT lon lat BYRADIUS radius M|KM|FT|MI | BYBOX width height M|KM|FT|MI [ASC|DESC] [COUNT count [ANY]] [WITHCOORD] [WITHDIST] [WITHHASH]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GEOSEARCH mygeo FROMLONLAT 15 37 BYRADIUS 200 km ASC</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "Catania"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "Palermo"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-teal-400">GEOSEARCHSTORE</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Like GEOSEARCH, but stores the results in a destination sorted set. With STOREDIST, stores the distance as the score instead of the geohash.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GEOSEARCHSTORE dest src FROMMEMBER member | FROMLONLAT lon lat BYRADIUS radius M|KM|FT|MI | BYBOX width height M|KM|FT|MI [ASC|DESC] [COUNT count [ANY]] [STOREDIST]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GEOSEARCHSTORE nearby mygeo FROMLONLAT 15 37 BYRADIUS 200 km ASC</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-teal-400">GEORADIUS / GEORADIUSBYMEMBER / GEORADIUS_RO / GEORADIUSBYMEMBER_RO</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">The pre-6.2 radius queries, kept for older clients; <code class="text-slate-300">GEOSEARCH</code> is the modern form.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">GEORADIUS key longitude latitude radius m|km|ft|mi [WITHCOORD] [WITHDIST] [WITHHASH] [COUNT n [ANY]] [ASC|DESC] [STORE key] [STOREDIST key]<br>GEORADIUSBYMEMBER key member radius m|km|ft|mi [...same options]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GEOADD sicily 13.361389 38.115556 Palermo 15.087269 37.502669 Catania</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GEORADIUS sicily 15 37 200 km ASC</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "Catania"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "Palermo"</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="server">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-slate-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold text-slate-400">*</span>
            Server, persistence, replication &amp; cluster
        </h2>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-slate-400">PING / ECHO / AUTH / HELLO / QUIT / RESET / SELECT / CLIENT</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Connection commands. <code class="text-slate-300">HELLO 3</code> switches the connection to RESP3. <code class="text-slate-300">CLIENT</code> covers <code class="text-slate-300">ID</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">SETNAME</code>/<code class="text-slate-300">GETNAME</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">SETINFO</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">LIST</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">INFO</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">KILL</code> (by <code class="text-slate-300">ID</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">ADDR</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">TYPE</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">USER</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">MAXAGE</code>), <code class="text-slate-300">PAUSE</code>/<code class="text-slate-300">UNPAUSE</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">UNBLOCK</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">REPLY</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">NO-EVICT</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">NO-TOUCH</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">TRACKING</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">CACHING</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">TRACKINGINFO</code> and <code class="text-slate-300">GETREDIR</code>.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">PING [message]<br>ECHO message<br>AUTH [username] password<br>HELLO [protover [AUTH username password] [SETNAME name]]<br>QUIT<br>RESET<br>SELECT index (0 … --databases − 1)<br>CLIENT subcommand [arguments]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">PING</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">PONG</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">CLIENT SETNAME worker-1</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">CLIENT GETNAME</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"worker-1"</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-slate-400">INFO / CONFIG / COMMAND / DBSIZE / FLUSHDB / FLUSHALL / SWAPDB / TIME / ACL / SLOWLOG / LATENCY / MEMORY / MONITOR / DEBUG</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Administration and diagnostics. <code class="text-slate-300">INFO</code> has every Redis section, including <code class="text-slate-300">commandstats</code> and <code class="text-slate-300">errorstats</code>. <code class="text-slate-300">CONFIG SET</code> changes the runtime-mutable parameters and <code class="text-slate-300">CONFIG REWRITE</code> writes them back to the config file. <code class="text-slate-300">DEBUG</code> is off unless the server runs with <code class="text-slate-300">--enable-debug-command</code>.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">INFO [section ...]<br>CONFIG GET pattern [pattern ...] | SET param value [...] | REWRITE | RESETSTAT<br>COMMAND [COUNT | INFO name ... | DOCS | LIST | GETKEYS ...]<br>DBSIZE<br>FLUSHDB [ASYNC|SYNC]<br>FLUSHALL [ASYNC|SYNC]<br>SWAPDB index1 index2<br>TIME<br>ACL SETUSER | GETUSER | DELUSER | LIST | USERS | WHOAMI | CAT | GENPASS | LOG | DRYRUN | SAVE | LOAD<br>SLOWLOG GET [count] | LEN | RESET<br>LATENCY LATEST | HISTORY event | RESET | DOCTOR<br>MEMORY USAGE key | STATS | DOCTOR<br>MONITOR</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ACL WHOAMI</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"default"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">CONFIG GET maxmemory</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "maxmemory"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "0"</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ACL SETUSER reader on &gt;secret ~cache:* +get +mget</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET k v</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">MEMORY USAGE k</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 66</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-slate-400">SAVE / BGSAVE / BGREWRITEAOF / LASTSAVE / SHUTDOWN</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Persistence. <code class="text-slate-300">BGSAVE</code> and <code class="text-slate-300">BGREWRITEAOF</code> return at once and work in the background; <code class="text-slate-300">SAVE</code> blocks the caller only. <code class="text-slate-300">SHUTDOWN</code> stops writes, fsyncs the log and snapshots unless <code class="text-slate-300">NOSAVE</code>. See <a href="/docs/persistence" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-white">Persistence</a>.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">SAVE<br>BGSAVE<br>BGREWRITEAOF<br>LASTSAVE<br>SHUTDOWN [NOSAVE | SAVE]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">BGSAVE</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">Background saving started</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-slate-400">REPLICAOF / ROLE / WAIT</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Replication. A replica does a full resynchronization, then follows the master's stream and resumes with a partial resync after a disconnect. <code class="text-slate-300">WAIT</code> blocks until that many replicas acknowledged the client's writes. See <a href="/docs/clustering" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-white">Replication &amp; Cluster</a>.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">REPLICAOF host port<br>REPLICAOF NO ONE<br>ROLE<br>WAIT numreplicas timeout-ms</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">On a replica, <span class="text-slate-400">ROLE</span> returns <span class="text-slate-400">"slave"</span>, the master's host and port, the link state (<span class="text-slate-400">connected</span>) and the replication offset.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ROLE</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "master"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) (integer) 0</div>
                <div class="text-white">3) (empty array)</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-8 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1 font-mono text-slate-400">CLUSTER / ASKING / READONLY / READWRITE / MIGRATE</h3>
            <div class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-3">Redis Cluster protocol (with <code class="text-slate-300">--cluster-enabled</code>). <code class="text-slate-300">CLUSTER</code> subcommands: <code class="text-slate-300">INFO</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">NODES</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">SLOTS</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">SHARDS</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">MYID</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">MYSHARDID</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">KEYSLOT</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">COUNTKEYSINSLOT</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">GETKEYSINSLOT</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">MEET</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">FORGET</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">ADDSLOTS</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">ADDSLOTSRANGE</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">DELSLOTS</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">DELSLOTSRANGE</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">FLUSHSLOTS</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">SETSLOT</code> (<code class="text-slate-300">IMPORTING</code>/<code class="text-slate-300">MIGRATING</code>/<code class="text-slate-300">STABLE</code>/<code class="text-slate-300">NODE</code>), <code class="text-slate-300">REPLICATE</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">REPLICAS</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">FAILOVER [FORCE|TAKEOVER]</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">RESET</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">SAVECONFIG</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">BUMPEPOCH</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">SET-CONFIG-EPOCH</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">COUNT-FAILURE-REPORTS</code>, <code class="text-slate-300">LINKS</code>.</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm text-slate-300 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mb-4">CLUSTER subcommand [arguments]<br>ASKING<br>READONLY<br>READWRITE<br>MIGRATE host port key|"" destination-db timeout [COPY] [REPLACE] [AUTH password | AUTH2 username password] [KEYS key ...]</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-sm bg-slate-900 rounded-lg p-4">
                <div class="text-slate-500"># On node 127.0.0.1:7000 of a three-master cluster</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:7000&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">CLUSTER KEYSLOT mykey</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 14687</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:7000&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">GET mykey</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(error) MOVED 14687 127.0.0.1:7002</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:7000&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">MSET a 1 b 2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(error) CROSSSLOT Keys in request don't hash to the same slot</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:7000&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">CLUSTER INFO</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">cluster_state:ok</div>
                <div class="text-white">cluster_slots_assigned:16384</div>
                <div class="text-white">cluster_known_nodes:6</div>
                <div class="text-white">cluster_size:3</div>
                <div class="text-white">...</div>
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>

    <!-- WRONGTYPE note -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-red-500/10 border border-red-500/30">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-red-400">Type Safety</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400">All typed commands check the key type first. Using a list command on a string key (or vice versa) returns:</p>
        <div class="font-mono text-sm text-red-400 bg-slate-900 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 mt-3">-WRONGTYPE Operation against a key holding the wrong kind of value</div>
    </div>
</div>
